Project structure and notes

- `includes/` — shared header/footer/sidebar files (used by pages)
- `temp/` — temporary artifacts that will be removed when you migrate to a database:
  - `temp/users.json` — file-based user store
  - `temp/seed_user.php` — script to seed a test user (dave)
- `register.php` — registration page (note: uses `temp/users.json` for now)
- `login.php`, `loginPage.php`, `logout.php`, `index.php` — core auth and dashboard pages

Notes:
- Duplicate root include files (header/footer/sidebar/seed_user.php and `data/users.json`) were moved to `temp/backup/` for safe cleanup; the canonical copies are in `includes/` and `temp/`.

Next steps:
- Migrate `temp/users.json` -> real database and remove `temp/` files
- Optionally move CSS into `includes/` or `public/` for better separation

